WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:07.040
House of the Dragon is the new Game of Thrones&nbsp;
prequel show. It's set two hundred years before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:12.960
Game of Thrones – and it’s about the Targaryen&nbsp;
family, Daenerys Targaryen’s ancestors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:19.120
back when they ruled Westeros at the height of&nbsp;
their power. This is a story of ambition and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:27.520
politics, betrayal and revenge, dragons, and a lot&nbsp;
of really angry blond people. The show is based on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:33.520
a book called Fire &amp; Blood, by George Martin.&nbsp;
George co-created this show with Ryan Condal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:38.880
and they say it’s a faithful adaptation of the&nbsp;
book. George has a nickname for House of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:45.600
Dragon – he calls it Hot D. There are a bunch&nbsp;
of new trailers and interviews out for Hot D,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:51.760
so what do they reveal, and what can we expect&nbsp;
from the new show? This video has no spoilers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:57.920
just introduces the characters and world.
So – quick history – the Targaryens are the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:04.560
royal dynasty of Westeros. But originally, the&nbsp;
Targaryens came from Valyria, the old empire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:10.880
of the dragonlords in the east. Valyria was&nbsp;
destroyed in the mysterious Doom of Valyria,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:16.320
and the Targaryens were the only dragon-riders to&nbsp;
survive – cause the Targaryens had already left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:24.160
Valyria, and settled on Dragonstone, an island off&nbsp;
Westeros. Aegon Targaryen, with his sister-wives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:30.240
and their dragons, conquered the Seven Kingdoms,&nbsp;
forged the Iron Throne, and became the first King&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:37.040
of Westeros. After him was King Aenys, then&nbsp;
King Maegor, then King Jaehaerys, and in House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:44.000
of the Dragon, the king is Viserys Targaryen.
The basic story in Hot D is that King Viserys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:49.440
wants his daughter, Princess Rhaenyra, to take&nbsp;
the Throne and rule after him. But some people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:55.760
have other plans for the Throne – including the&nbsp;
king’s brother Daemon, and the King’s Hand Otto,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:02.400
and Otto’s daughter Alicent. But this conflict&nbsp;
builds up slowly, with tensions rising over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:07.680
years and years. So Hot D occasionally&nbsp;
jumps forward in time several years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:13.200
to show how the politics and relationships&nbsp;
gradually change. Alicent and Rhaenyra are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:19.600
played by different actors as they age – like&nbsp;
in The Crown. Co-creator Ryan Condal said this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:25.600
is “a generational war” – and the time span lets&nbsp;
us fully understand these characters, and their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:33.840
history, before the “first sword stroke falls”.
So Viserys Targaryen is king, and he inherited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:40.480
a peaceful and prosperous realm from Jaehaerys.&nbsp;
So Viserys’ reign became the apex of Targaryen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:46.800
power and wealth. That’s reflected in the size&nbsp;
of the Iron Throne in Hot D – it’s bigger and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:52.000
grander – compared to how it looks in Game of&nbsp;
Thrones. The new design is also closer to how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:59.040
the Throne is described in the books – as a huge&nbsp;
monstrosity of metal, forged from the swords of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:06.800
King Aegon’s enemies. In Game of Thrones, dragons&nbsp;
are almost extinct. But in Hot D, the Targaryens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:13.840
have lots of dragons, and that’s how they dominate&nbsp;
Westeros. Dragons are weapons of mass destruction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:19.200
they’re like the nuclear bombs of this world,&nbsp;
and since only the Targaryens have dragons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:25.680
no one can mess with them. When Viserys was&nbsp;
younger, he rode the dragon Balerion, the biggest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:32.080
and baddest Targaryen dragon. But Balerion&nbsp;
soon died of old age, and Viserys hasn’t ridden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:38.720
a dragon since. In a trailer, he calls dragons&nbsp;
“a power man should never have trifled with”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:45.280
like they’re too dangerous to be controlled.
Cause King Viserys is “a man of peace”, he just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:51.440
wants everyone to get along and have a good time.&nbsp;
So he hosts feasts, and balls and tournaments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:57.920
he’s popular with the lords and common folk.&nbsp;
Viserys is a good man. But being a good man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:03.760
doesn’t make you a good king. And times&nbsp;
of peace can sow the seeds of war.&nbsp;

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:10.640
In a trailer, Viserys describes a dream&nbsp;
of his heir, and the Throne, and dragons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:15.920
In the books, many Targaryens have prophetic&nbsp;
dragon dreams that can tell the future.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:21.360
But often these dreams are.. misinterpreted&nbsp;
and lead to the dreamer’s downfall – Aemon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:28.000
Targaryen says his brothers dreamed of dragons,&nbsp;
and those dreams “killed them, every one”.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:35.280
Dragon dreams can be a metaphor for ambition&nbsp;
and the dangers of ambition. Viserys’ actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:42.480
Paddy Considine says that Viserys has an ego, and&nbsp;
he wants a legacy – “there is a dragon in him”.&nbsp;

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:48.640
So Viserys is a complicated guy. Author George&nbsp;
Martin said he’s impressed with Considine’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:53.600
performance, giving Viserys a “tragic&nbsp;
majesty” that he never had in the books.&nbsp;

00:04:54.560 --> 00:05:01.120
One of the biggest problems for Viserys is his&nbsp;
brother, Prince Daemon Targaryen. Daemon is like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:07.120
the opposite of Viserys. Cause while Viserys&nbsp;
is peaceful, Daemon is violent and impulsive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:13.920
Actor Matt Smith said “Daemon is there to cause&nbsp;
chaos and piss people off”. Daemon rides the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:20.320
red dragon Caraxes, called “the Blood Wyrm”, and&nbsp;
Daemon’s personality is reflected in his dragon’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:28.160
personality – Caraxes is “like a huge rabid&nbsp;
dog”, volatile and chaotic. There are at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:34.080
17 dragons in this story – and the showrunners&nbsp;
say we’ll meet nine of them in Season 1.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:39.920
Each dragon has a distinct personality,&nbsp;
colour, and look – some of them are “bearded,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:47.760
like tropical lizards”. Apparently Caraxes is a&nbsp;
“deformed” dragon with a super long neck and extra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:53.680
wings on his hind legs. These unique designs&nbsp;
contrast with the dragons in Game of Thrones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:59.600
which were almost impossible to tell apart –&nbsp;
despite their colourful descriptions in the books.&nbsp;

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:06.240
Prince Daemon is a great warrior. He&nbsp;
wields the legendary Valyrian steel sword&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:12.080
Dark Sister, once used by Queen Visenya&nbsp;
– and used by King Maegor the Cruel.&nbsp;

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:17.120
In the trailers, we see Daemon leading&nbsp;
the City Watch of King’s Landing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:23.040
called the gold cloaks – we saw the gold cloaks&nbsp;
in Game of Thrones betraying Ned in Season 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:30.160
and buying.. crab aphrodisiacs in Season 7.&nbsp;
Cause Daemon is Commander of the City Watch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:33.680
and he’s the one who first gave&nbsp;
the Watch their gold cloaks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:39.920
and better armour – so Daemon is why they’re&nbsp;
now called gold cloaks. Daemon gets real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:46.480
enthusiastic about law enforcement – especially&nbsp;
the part where you cut body parts off criminals.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:52.480
As Commander of the Watch, he’s known as the&nbsp;
“Prince of the City” or “Lord Flea Bottom”.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:59.760
Daemon has an estranged wife called Rhea Royce&nbsp;
who he hates, and calls his “bronze bitch”.&nbsp;

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:06.000
Daemon considers himself heir to the Throne,&nbsp;
after Viserys. But Viserys doesn’t want him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:11.600
on the Throne because he’s such a loose&nbsp;
cannon. Daemon does act sometimes like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:18.400
just a violent villainous dickhead, but there&nbsp;
are layers to him, and sensitivity. Deep down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:23.920
despite their differences, Daemon and Viserys&nbsp;
love each other, and what Daemon really wants is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:30.720
approval and recognition from his brother. The&nbsp;
books say that Daemon is a hero and a villain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:40.640
a “rogue prince” made of both light and darkness.
Princess Rhaenyra is Viserys’ beloved only child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:46.720
and he wants her to inherit his Throne. He keeps&nbsp;
her by his side at council so she can learn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:52.880
politics. Rhaenyra is precocious, beautiful,&nbsp;
and popular at court – singers call her “the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.880 --> 00:08:00.960
Realm’s Delight”. Rhaenyra has been a dragonrider&nbsp;
since age 7, bonded with the yellow dragon Syrax.&nbsp;

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:06.160
We can see that Targaryens now use saddles to ride&nbsp;
their dragons, which looks a lot more comfortable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:13.040
than Daenerys did clinging to Drogon’s scaly back&nbsp;
in Game of Thrones. In Hot D, the dragons are kept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:19.200
at this building called the Dragonpit. And there’s&nbsp;
tradition around dragon eggs – baby Targaryens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:24.720
often have dragon eggs put in their cribs, so that&nbsp;
they bond with the dragons that hatch from them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:31.120
The Targaryens have close relationships with&nbsp;
their dragons – possibly too close historically.&nbsp;

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:38.720
But Rhaenyra has that oldschool Targaryen fiery&nbsp;
personality. Her actor Emma D’Arcy says Rhaenyra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:45.920
“has to learn when to dampen that fire and when to&nbsp;
trust it” – Rhaenyra has similarities to Daenerys.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:52.480
You can also compare Rhaenyra to Arya, with her&nbsp;
“rebellious and cheeky spirit”, and her conflict&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:59.040
against society’s gender roles. In the patriarchal&nbsp;
world of Westeros, many lords don’t want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:05.440
a woman on the Throne. There’s never been a female&nbsp;
ruler of Westeros, and the rules of succession&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:11.920
prefer men to women. So Rhaenyra feels a constant&nbsp;
“battle with what it means to be a woman”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:18.560
and how her gender clashes with her political&nbsp;
power – which a similar theme to Cersei’s story.&nbsp;

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:26.480
Rhaenyra’s best friend is Alicent Hightower, the&nbsp;
daughter of the Hand of the King, Otto Hightower.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:32.880
While Rhaenyra is rebellious, Alicent tends to&nbsp;
follow the rules, and do what’s expected of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:39.760
noble lady – kinda like Sansa Stark. In Hot D,&nbsp;
Alicent and Rhaenyra grow up together at court,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:45.120
and they’re super close, like siblings. Which&nbsp;
is a change from the books – in the books,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:51.200
Alicent is older than Rhaenyra, and we don’t know&nbsp;
much about her childhood. The book, Fire &amp; Blood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:57.680
gives only a broad summary of these events. So&nbsp;
it’s up to the show Hot D, to create much of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:04.480
detail of these relationships and personalities.
Alicent came to court with her father, Otto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:10.720
Hightower. Otto is Hand of the King, so he’s like&nbsp;
the second most powerful person in Westeros – like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:15.360
how Ned Stark and Tywin Lannister were&nbsp;
Hand of the King in Game of Thrones.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:22.080
Otto’s family, the Hightowers, are one of the&nbsp;
oldest and richest houses in Westeros. They rule&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:28.240
the city of Oldtown, home of the maesters of the&nbsp;
Citadel and of the High Septon of the Faith of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:35.920
the Seven. The Hightowers tend to avoid war, and&nbsp;
gain power through trade and politics. In Hot D,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:42.320
the Lord of Oldtown is Hobert Hightower – he&nbsp;
rules the city, while his brother Otto is at court&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:49.920
as Hand of the King. Otto is a smart strategic&nbsp;
politician, “a pragmatist and a manipulator”.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:57.040
He’s proud, ambitious and “ruthless” but he also&nbsp;
“struggles” with his decisions. Otto loves his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.040 --> 00:11:03.200
daughter Alicent, but they don’t communicate well,&nbsp;
and their relationship is complicated by politics.&nbsp;

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:10.080
Otto hates Prince Daemon, and wants to prevent him&nbsp;
from having power. So Otto and Daemon are always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:16.000
competing for influence over King Viserys.
As well as the Hightowers, another important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:22.480
family is House Velaryon, led by Lord&nbsp;
Corlys, the Sea Snake. Like the Targaryens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:28.640
the Velaryons originally came from Valyria in the&nbsp;
east. But unlike the Targaryens, the Velaryons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:35.360
aren’t dragon riders. Instead, they love sailing,&nbsp;
and have a powerful fleet of ships. They’re based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:41.440
on Driftmark, an island near Dragonstone and&nbsp;
King’s Landing – and they’re close allies of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:48.480
Targaryens – ruling the seas, while the Targaryens&nbsp;
on their dragons rule the skies. Lord Corlys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:56.240
Velaryon is a famous adventurer and explorer. He’s&nbsp;
sailed to far-distant places like Qarth, Yi Ti&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.240 --> 00:12:02.960
and Asshai. By trading with these exotic places,&nbsp;
Corlys has made the Velaryons the richest family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:09.040
in Westeros, even richer than the Lannisters&nbsp;
and Hightowers. Corlys has seen the world and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:15.840
made a fortune, but he’s still not satisfied&nbsp;
– Corlys has great ambitions for his family.&nbsp;

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:21.920
In Hot D, Corlys and his family are black –&nbsp;
which is a change from the books. In the books,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:26.960
the Velaryons look like the Targaryens, cause&nbsp;
the two families have been marrying each other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:33.440
for generations. The Targaryens like to keep&nbsp;
their Valyrian dragon blood in the family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:37.680
so when they don’t marry a Velaryon,&nbsp;
they usually marry their sister – so the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:45.120
Targaryens and Velaryons in books are one big&nbsp;
incestuous family of inbred blondes. In Hot D,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:51.680
they’ve changed the look. But the Velaryons still&nbsp;
have silver hair, indicating the Valyrian blood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:56.960
that they share with the Targaryens.
After Corlys’ voyages across the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:04.640
he got married – to Princess Rhaenys Targaryen.
Rhaenys is a cousin of Viserys and Daemon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:11.360
Rhaenys’ mother was a Baratheon, so in the in the&nbsp;
books, Rhaenys has black hair. Rhaenys is “fierce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:18.320
and fearless”, “proud”, smart, and capable.&nbsp;
She’s been a dragonrider since she was thirteen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:24.560
riding “Meleys, the Red Queen”. When Rhaenys&nbsp;
married Corlys, she arrived at the wedding on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:29.680
dragonback. Corlys said “I came back&nbsp;
from the ends of the earth for you”.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:35.280
And Rhaenys said “We can go back to the ends of&nbsp;
the earth together”, “But I’ll get there first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:41.120
as I’ll be flying”. Rhaenys and Corlys&nbsp;
have a deep love, and one of the more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:48.320
healthy relationships in the story. But Rhaenys&nbsp;
and Corlys also have ambition, and resentment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:54.640
Because Rhaenys was the firstborn child of King&nbsp;
Jaehaerys’ firstborn son – so back in the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.640 --> 00:14:00.560
many people saw Rhaenys as the rightful heir&nbsp;
to the Throne. But male rulers are preferred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:06.640
over women. So King Jaehaerys repeatedly passed&nbsp;
over Rhaenys to make his second son Baelon and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:14.480
then Baelon’s son Viserys the heir instead. So&nbsp;
Rhaenys is called the Queen who never was. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:19.680
and Corlys feel that her birthright, and her&nbsp;
childrens’ birthright, was taken from her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:27.280
And this injustice hasn’t been forgotten.
Corlys and Rhaenys have two children, Laena&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:33.200
and Laenor Velaryon. Laena is “fiery”&nbsp;
and “adventurous” like her parents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:39.600
and she rides Vhagar, the biggest and&nbsp;
oldest dragon alive. While Laenor rides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:46.320
the “splendid grey-and-white dragon” Seasmoke.
So those are the three important families in House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:52.480
of the Dragon. The Targaryens – with King Viserys,&nbsp;
his daughter Rhaenyra, and brother Daemon. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:58.640
Hightowers, with Otto and his daughter Alicent.&nbsp;
And the Velaryons, with Corlys, his wife Rhaenys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:04.720
and their kids Laena and Laenor. But there&nbsp;
are a few other important characters at court.&nbsp;

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:10.720
Criston Cole is not a prince or a lord from a&nbsp;
great house – he’s the son of a steward. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:17.840
he is a talented fighter – and he’s dangerously&nbsp;
hot – “a favorite of all the ladies at court”.&nbsp;

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:25.120
Mysaria is a woman from a brothel in Lys. In&nbsp;
the books she’s described as a “very pale”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:33.120
“older woman”, sometimes called “Misery, the White&nbsp;
Worm”. Mysaria is a lover and trusted confident of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:39.840
Prince Daemon. In Hot D, she’s described as&nbsp;
a survivor with street smarts and ambition.&nbsp;

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:47.440
Lyonel Strong is the Lord of Harrenhal – that&nbsp;
giant half-ruined castle in the riverlands.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:54.720
Lyonel serves on King Viserys’ council as the&nbsp;
master of laws. He’s a big man, with a reputation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:54.720 --> 00:16:01.920
as a warrior, and some people assume he’s a dumb&nbsp;
brute. But Lyonel is very intelligent, having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:08.960
studied at the Citadel. He brings his sons Harwin&nbsp;
“Breakbones” and Larys “the Clubfoot” to court.&nbsp;

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:15.760
And this guy is Grand Maester Mellos. He advises&nbsp;
the king as representative of the Citadel of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:22.640
maester, like Grand Maester Pycelle in Game of&nbsp;
Thrones. Mellos is described as a voice for peace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:27.440
“urging calm and compromise”, and is&nbsp;
a “trusted friend” of King Viserys.&nbsp;

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:34.320
Maesters are meant to be unbiased servants,&nbsp;
working for the good of the realm. But some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:39.920
characters in the books don’t trust the&nbsp;
maesters – Tyrion says the gods only know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:45.680
who they’re “conspiring with”, or what they&nbsp;
mix into their potions. Another character says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.680 --> 00:16:51.760
they could be twisting the words of the letters&nbsp;
they read and write for their lords. In Book 5,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:56.960
this guy Marwyn claims that for centuries,&nbsp;
the maesters have secretly worked against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:56.960 --> 00:17:03.760
the Targaryens, to kill off all their dragons.&nbsp;
There’s no proof of any of this in the books,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:11.040
and Marwyn is kind of a crazy conspiracy theorist.&nbsp;
But if we look closely, Hot D may have hints of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:18.000
the maesters manipulating politics. Ultimately,&nbsp;
it’s the maesters who write the history books,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:24.000
and in Fire &amp; Blood, author George Martin plays&nbsp;
with the idea of bias in historical sources.&nbsp;

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:29.840
The main Game of Thrones books are novels,&nbsp;
told from the point of view of the characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:36.560
in the moment. But Fire &amp; Blood is different –&nbsp;
it’s s a fictional history book, written by an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:43.200
in-world historian called Archmaester Gyldayn.&nbsp;
Gyldayn wrote Fire &amp; Blood years after the events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:48.880
he’s describing, so he relies on historical&nbsp;
sources that are sometimes contradictory.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:55.520
Two of his sources for the story of Hot D&nbsp;
are a septon called Eustace, a dwarf jester&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:55.520 --> 00:18:01.600
called Mushroom. While Eustace’s version of&nbsp;
the story is very proper and straightforward,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:07.680
Mushroom’s version is full of bloody murder&nbsp;
and secret scandalous sex. And it’s up to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:14.240
reader to decide whose version of the story&nbsp;
is true. Hot D can only show one version of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:20.400
events – it’ll be the “objective” account of what&nbsp;
really happened. But we can compare Hot D to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:28.080
stories in Fire &amp; Blood to see whether Eustace was&nbsp;
right, or if Mushroom’s scandalous tales are true.&nbsp;

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:32.960
One of the problems with the Game of Thrones&nbsp;
show is that the book series it’s based on isn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:39.040
finished. Thrones ran out of books to adapt in&nbsp;
Season 5, and that’s when the show started getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:55.440
worse. Fortunately, Hot D is different, because&nbsp;
the book it’s based on, Fire &amp; Blood, tells the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:55.440 --> 00:19:02.080
full story of this conflict from beginning to end.&nbsp;
So the writers know where they’re going this time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:07.440
And George Martin is much more involved&nbsp;
than he was in the last seasons of Thrones.&nbsp;

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:14.800
Hot D is a fantasy, but it’s not about&nbsp;
black-and-white heroes-and-villains. Author George&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:21.760
Martin loves “grey characters”, who have both&nbsp;
good and evil in them. Like, in Game of Thrones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:28.160
the Starks are mostly heroic, and the Lannisters&nbsp;
are.. mostly villainous, but they’re complicated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:35.440
right? Well Hot D is even more morally ambiguous.&nbsp;
Viewers will have different opinions on who the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:43.040
heroes and the villains are in this story. These&nbsp;
are complex, conflicted characters, who hurt each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:51.040
other in spectacularly messy ways. There’ll be&nbsp;
high drama, cheating, lies, revenge – “dark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:59.200
turbulent, bloody doings”. And we’ll cover it&nbsp;
all with videos each week, so like and subscribe.&nbsp;

